Article [10](/lagstiftning/red/kap-2#article-10-obligations-of-manufacturers)(10)

STATEMENT OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT

The European Parliament considers that only when and insofar as implementing acts in the sense of [Regulation (EU) No 182/2011](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011R0182) are discussed in meetings of committees, can the latter be considered as ‘comitology committees’ within the meaning of Annex I to the Framework Agreement on the relations between the European Parliament and the European Commission. Meetings of committees thus fall within the scope of point 15 of the Framework Agreement when and insofar as other issues are discussed.
<!-- scan-laws:end -->

